---
import {mediaUrl} from '../data/brain/teaching-library';
---
<section class="guitar-learning" data-salience-selection aria-label="Salience and posterior parietal stimulation">
  <div class="salience-choices">
    <label>Stimulus bias<select data-salience-bias><option value="global">Global stands out</option><option value="local">Local stands out</option></select></label>
    <label>Task instruction<select data-salience-target><option value="global">Name the global letter</option><option value="local">Name the local letter</option></select></label>
    <label>Comparison condition<select data-salience-condition><option value="pre">Pre-TMS</option><option value="left">Left PPC TMS</option><option value="right">Right PPC TMS</option></select></label>
  </div>
  <div class="learning-screen">
    <svg class="learning-circuit salience-diagram" viewBox="0 0 1280 650" role="img" aria-labelledby="salience-title salience-desc">
      <title id="salience-title">Selecting more or less salient information</title><desc id="salience-desc">The original lecture stimulus and results graph. Global or local selects letter scale; bias determines which stands out. Higher mean interference indicates worse performance.</desc>
      <text x="48" y="32" class="diagram-eyebrow">SALIENCE-BASED SELECTION · L14</text><text x="48" y="77" class="diagram-heading" data-salience-heading>Set the task and comparison</text>
      <g data-salience-setup>
        <image data-salience-stimulus="global" href={mediaUrl('interaction-global-bias.png','l14')} x="140" y="122" width="390" height="470"/>
        <image data-salience-stimulus="local" href={mediaUrl('interaction-local-bias.png','l14')} x="140" y="122" width="390" height="470" visibility="hidden"/>
        <text x="660" y="185" class="salience-key">TASK</text><text x="660" y="227" class="salience-value" data-salience-task>Name the global letter: H</text>
        <text x="660" y="301" class="salience-key">TARGET SALIENCE</text><text x="660" y="343" class="salience-value" data-salience-level>More salient</text>
        <text x="660" y="417" class="salience-key">COMPARISON</text><text x="660" y="459" class="salience-value" data-salience-comparison>Pre-TMS reference</text>
      </g>
      <g data-salience-evidence display="none">
        <image href={mediaUrl('interaction-salience-results.png','l14')} x="48" y="118" width="632" height="480"/>
        <text x="725" y="193" class="salience-key" data-salience-evidence-target>More-salient target</text>
        <text x="725" y="244" class="salience-value" data-salience-evidence-condition>Pre-TMS reference</text>
        <text x="725" y="321" class="salience-result" data-salience-result>Reference performance</text>
        <text x="725" y="437" class="salience-note">Higher interference = worse</text><text x="725" y="474" class="salience-note">Read the matching group of bars.</text>
      </g>
      <text x="48" y="632" class="diagram-note">PPC = posterior parietal cortex · TMS temporarily interferes with regional function.</text>
    </svg>
    <div class="learning-caption" aria-live="polite"><span data-salience-stage>SETUP</span><p data-salience-caption>Choose the stimulus bias, task and comparison; then reveal the study result.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="learning-controls"><button type="button" data-salience-reveal>Reveal study result</button><button type="button" data-salience-reset>↺ Reset</button><button type="button" data-illustration-fullscreen>⛶ Fullscreen</button></div>
  <p class="learning-limit">Findings apply to this study’s task. The graph shows the original evidence, not a measurement of the viewer’s performance.</p>
</section>
<style>
  .salience-choices{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0 0 18px}.salience-choices label{font-size:12px;color:#a9c2cc;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}.salience-choices select{background:#102735;color:#eafaff;border:1px solid #365563;border-radius:3px;padding:8px;max-width:100%}.salience-key{font-size:22px;font-weight:600;fill:#536373}.salience-value{font-size:28px;font-weight:600;fill:#1d3552}.salience-result{font-size:25px;fill:#1d3552}.salience-note{font-size:22px;fill:#536373}
</style>
